  "body": "Stacked on #2243. The base is `issue/2235-selection-frame-cost`. Retarget this PR to `main` before #2243 merges.\n\n## What changed\n\n- New `crates/ui/src/frame_cost.rs`: named spans. A span is a no-op flag read unless a probe records. Nothing reads a span to decide what to draw.\n- Spans on the pieces of a frame:\n  - `commands/*` in `State::drain_actions`;\n  - `scene/parts.*` and `scene/overlay.*` in `world.rs` and `interact.rs`;\n  - `ui/*` in `shell.rs`, `op_page.rs`, `geo_page.rs`, `params_page.rs` and `boundary.rs`.\n- New probe test `egui_app::tests::frame_cost_probe::still_frames_on_fig8_name_their_costs`. It loads fig8.step, makes five states and measures six still frames in each. It asserts counts only, never times.\n- `docs/decisions/2238-frame-cost-rule.md`: the cache rule (key order, the writer invalidates, the layer, two tests for each cache, the safety line, simulation keyframes).\n- `crates/ui/AGENTS.md`: a short \"Frame cost\" section that cites the decision.\n- `testdata/models/fig8.step`: taken unchanged from `main` (commit 6cf7cf991, #2215), because the #2243 base does not have it.\n\nNo behaviour change. No change to chains, cut geometry, posted G-code or goldens.\n\n## Readings (release, ms for each still frame, fig8.step, 1600 x 1000)\n\n| State | commands | scene | UI | Total | Largest pieces |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| a nothing selected | 0.00 | 1.47 | 2.00 | 3.5 | `ui/viewport.labels` 0.62 |\n| b Contour on 10 top chains | 0.01 | 1.64 | 11.44 | 13.1 | `selection_account` 4.24, `contour_auto_side` 4.13 |\n| c 2D Adaptive, Outside, area preview | 0.01 | 18.20 | 11.84 | 30.0 | `boundary_preview.triangulate` 15.12, `picks.chips` 4.68, `align_321` 1.98, `overlay.selection_features` 1.48, `selection_account` 1.22 |\n| d Face toolpath shown | 0.00 | 1.15 | 2.19 | 3.3 | `scene/overlay.toolpaths` 0.28 |\n| e simulation paused | 0.00 | 1.20 | 2.19 | 3.4 | as d |\n\nEach named piece runs one time for each frame. Idle frames do not repaint (`state_redraw_delay` gives `None`). No chain walk, digest or pocket slice on a still frame in any state.\n\n## Sub-issues (recommended order)\n\n1. #2246 (comment with the cause): the area preview triangulates its region on each frame, 15.1 ms.\n2. #2247: pick chips and the 3-2-1 check, 6.7 ms.\n3. #2248: `selection_account`, 4.2 ms.\n4. #2249: `contour_auto_side`, 4.1 ms.\n5. #2250: overlay lines of the picked features, 1.5 ms.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: 958 passed, 6 ignored (debug, `--test-threads=4`).\n- `frame_cost::tests::spans_count_only_while_recording`, `frame_cost_probe::still_frames_on_fig8_name_their_costs`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The real window: GPU upload, present and vsync are not measured. The probe is headless.\n- The hover path (no pointer moves) and the growth with the number of operations (#2201).\n- The browser tree with many operations; with four operations it costs 0.5 ms.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: max\nProcess change: yes\n\nRefs #2238\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
